# Pairs with LivePublisherPinned. Issue #4700's ordering reversed: the purge
# retires the leaf's pins when it commits, before the row clear, so an interrupted
# purge that recovery hands back leaves a live leaf with no pin.
MODULE: LivePublisherPinnedPurgeRetiresPinFirst
TARGET: LivePublisherPinned
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the purge retires the pins before it clears the row
PERTURBS: MarkPurge

--- FIND
    /\ phase' = "marked"
    /\ purgeMark' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED walVars
    /\ UNCHANGED <<inc, seeded, cp, need, owed, route>>
    /\ UNCHANGED pinVars
--- REPLACE
    /\ phase' = "marked"
    /\ purgeMark' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED walVars
    /\ UNCHANGED <<inc, seeded, cp, need, owed, route>>
\* MUTATION: the pins go at the mark.
    /\ pinOff' = [pinOff EXCEPT ![route, "cL"] = NoPin]
    /\ UNCHANGED pinInc
--- END
